# feh has no config file; this themes file is the only way to set defaults.
# A theme named after argv[0] ("feh") applies automatically to every launch,
# including desktop-file launches (Exec=feh --start-at %u).
#
# Fullscreen comes from sway (rules: [class="feh"] fullscreen), NOT from feh's
# own --fullscreen: under XWayland feh's first render centers the image against
# twice the real screen size, so the image lands at +w/2+h/2 (bottom-right).
# Only a resize event makes feh re-render with correct geometry, and
# --fullscreen never produces one. --geometry seeds a smaller window so sway's
# fullscreen always triggers that resize, including for screenshots that are
# already exactly screen-sized.
#
# --geometry    initial window size (also enables auto-zoom, like fullscreen)
# --auto-zoom   fit whole image in the window (never crops)
# --scale-down  shrink oversized images if zoom is reset (v key)
feh --geometry 1280x720 --auto-zoom --scale-down
